    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/55264>;
    <https://schema.org/text> "We see from this, then, that what we have called an anticlinal partition, as _MP_, is only likely to occur in a triangular or prismatic cell whose angle of arc lies between 90° and 62½°. In all narrower or more tapering cells, the periclinal partition will be of less area, and will therefore be more and more likely to occur.".
